title: Your own kinds of things
card: Chapter 7 | Your own kinds of things | Describing things with parts
say:
  Numbers, text and lists go a long way. But programs are usually about things: pets, players, coins, enemies.
  Fathom lets you describe a new kind of thing, and the parts it has.
uncard

new: pets.fathom
type:
  a pet has:
    name (text)
    age (a number)
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    set tom to conjure a pet
    set the name of tom to "Tom"
    set the age of tom to 3
    scrawl tom
    scrawl the name of tom, " is ", the age of tom, "."
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 1-4
say:
  A pet has: a name, which is text, and an age, which is a number. One part per line, each with its kind in brackets.
zoom: lines 6-12
spot: line 7
say:
  Conjure a pet makes a new pet. Its numbers start at zero, and its text starts empty.
spot: lines 8-9
say: The name of tom is one of tom's parts. Set changes it.
spot: lines 10-11
say: Scrawl tom shows the whole pet, with its parts. And the name of tom is just that part.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 7 | Commands for a kind | Things a pet can do
say:
  A command can belong to a kind of thing. Inside it, the thing's parts are used by their own names.
uncard
line: 4
type:

  
  to have a birthday, for a pet:
    set age to age plus 1
  and the universe said i love you
line: 15
type:

    have a birthday tom
    scrawl the name of tom, " is ", the age of tom, " now."
zoom: lines 6-8
spot: line 6
say: To have a birthday, for a pet. This command belongs to pets.
spot: line 7
say:
  Inside it, age means this pet's age. And changing it changes the pet it was given, not a copy.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
say: Tom was three, and after his birthday, he's four.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 7 | Kinds of kinds | A dog is a kind of pet
say:
  Now let's go further. A dog is a kind of pet: it has everything a pet has, and more. Here's a bigger program, and we'll go through it piece by piece.
uncard
clear
paste:
  a pet has:
    name (text)
    age (a number)
  and the universe said i love you

  a dog is a kind of pet that has:
    tricks (a list of text)
  and the universe said i love you

  a robot has:
    model (text)
  and the universe said i love you

  a speaker is anything that can speak.

  to speak, for a pet, returning text:
    return name plus " makes a sound."
  and the universe said i love you

  to speak, for a dog, returning text:
    return name plus " barks and knows " plus (the size of tricks) plus " tricks."
  and the universe said i love you

  to speak, for a robot, returning text:
    return "Beep, I am " plus model plus "."
  and the universe said i love you

  to have a birthday, for a pet:
    set age to age plus 1
  and the universe said i love you

  to the oldest, given pets (a list of pets), returning a pet:
    set best to no pet
    for each p in pets:
      if best is nothing or the age of p exceeds the age of best: set best to p
    return best
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    set tom to conjure a pet
    set the name of tom to "Tom"
    set the age of tom to 3
    scrawl tom
    have a birthday tom
    scrawl the name of tom, " is ", the age of tom, " now."
    conjure a dog as rex
    set the name of rex to "Rex"
    add "sit" to the tricks of rex
    conjure a robot as bolt
    set the model of bolt to "R2"
    set talkers to a list of speakers
    add tom to talkers
    add rex to talkers
    add bolt to talkers
    for each t in talkers: scrawl speak t
    set nobody to the oldest with a list of pets
    if nobody is nothing: scrawl "No pets, so nobody is oldest."
    scrawl the oldest with a list containing tom
  and the universe said i love you
line: 1
zoom: lines 6-8
say:
  A dog is a kind of pet that has tricks. So a dog has a name and an age, because every pet does, and a list of tricks as well.
zoom: lines 16-22
spot: lines 16-18
say: Speak, for a pet, returns some text: the pet's name, and makes a sound.
spot: lines 20-22
say:
  And speak, for a dog, is the dog's own version. Dogs use this one instead. Every other kind of pet uses the first.
spot: off
zoom: lines 10-14
spot: lines 10-12
say: A robot is not a pet at all. But it can speak too, in its own way.
spot: line 14
say:
  So this line makes a new kind, called a speaker: anything that can speak. Any kind of thing with its own speak command counts. Pets, dogs, and robots are all speakers.
spot: off
line: 59
zoom: lines 50-55
say:
  So a list of speakers can hold a pet, a dog and a robot together. And speak t does the speaking the way that kind of thing does it, while the program runs.
zoom: out
line: 32
zoom: lines 32-37
spot: line 33
say:
  One more idea: nothing. Best starts as no pet. A name for a kind of thing can hold nothing, when there isn't one.
spot: line 35
say: And is nothing, or is something, asks which. This command finds the oldest pet, and if there are no pets, it gives back nothing.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
say: Tom makes a sound. Rex barks. The robot beeps. And with no pets, nobody is oldest.
wait
zoom: out
